# <%= projectName %>

Rust walking skeleton scaffolded by keel — hexagonal, one package, no
mediator object: commands are structs, driving ports are per-use-case
traits, and each `src/bin/` main is the assembly point.

## Layout

```
src/bin/        — one directory per deployment unit: main.rs wires
                  the hexagon by hand (constructor injection); its
                  sibling modules are the unit's primary adapter —
                  transport → command → port → transport, zero
                  business logic
src/domain.rs   — the contract face: commands, ports, and the
                  exported factories returning driving ports
src/domain/     — the domain's submodules: the compiler-hidden core
                  (declared private in domain.rs, unnameable from
                  adapters and deployment units) and the port
                  modules the face re-exports
src/infra/      — secondary adapters, one module per technology;
                  each port's canonical fake lives here too
tests/          — DIP-strict tests against the crate's public face
```

Cross-cutting concerns (logging, metrics, tx) wrap the driving ports
as decorators applied at the assembly point.

## Test

```sh
cargo test
```

## Deployment units

Each `src/bin/` directory is one deployment unit; its `main.rs`
`use` list reads like the ops runbook.
